(474250, 44505, 13336, '<td valign="top">nice use of negative space - i like the angle of the subject and the eay the strap comes back into frame to brake up the space in the bottom left corner.  however, the subject doesn''t really get any kind of response from me.  i think that is the difference between a still life and a nice picture of an inanimate object.  but well done all the same.  it get a 6 from me - would have been higher if i had an emotional response from it.</td>', 'nice use of negative space - i like the angle of the subject and the eay the strap comes back into frame to brake up the space in the bottom left corner.  however, the subject doesn''t really get any kind of response from me.  i think that is the difference between a still life and a nice picture of an inanimate object.  but well done all the same.  it get a 6 from me - would have been higher if i had an emotional response from it.', '2003-11-05 17:04:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(474255, 45355, 13336, '<td valign="top">interesting use of negative space.  i''m on the fence about the sepia tone here.  part of me thinks it works, part of me thinks it only serves to dull this image.  maybe a white backround to further accent the sensuality of the subject?</td>', 'interesting use of negative space.  i''m on the fence about the sepia tone here.  part of me thinks it works, part of me thinks it only serves to dull this image.  maybe a white backround to further accent the sensuality of the subject?', '2003-11-05 17:07:41.000000', NULL, 1),
