(481649, 45351, 12589, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by G4Ds:</b></div><hr/><i>There seems to be a loss of resolution making the image appear blurry. I like the composition, but the light could be a little softer.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re right! I relly have porblems with resizing the photo, and makin git lower then 150kB. :(<br/>I allways loose "information" my photos became little blurry, even if I use the "100% quality" option when saving the newly sized photo. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by G4Ds:There seems to be a loss of resolution making the image appear blurry. I like the composition, but the light could be a little softer.  You''re right! I relly have porblems with resizing the photo, and makin git lower then 150kB. :(I allways loose "information" my photos became little blurry, even if I use the "100% quality" option when saving the newly sized photo.  ', '2003-11-12 04:40:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(481650, 45351, 12589, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Twocentz:</b></div><hr/><i>I was going to say the pink is a little harsh, but I actually like it very vibrant like that. Makes it really stand out against the black background. Did you use some sort of effect on it? I would have liked it a little sharper. But it still looks good.  =)</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>With the sharpness I can tell you the same as before.. I loose quality when I resize the photo. :( <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Twocentz:I was going to say the pink is a little harsh, but I actually like it very vibrant like that. Makes it really stand out against the black background. Did you use some sort of effect on it? I would have liked it a little sharper. But it still looks good.  =)  With the sharpness I can tell you the same as before.. I loose quality when I resize the photo. :(  ', '2003-11-12 04:41:26.000000', NULL, 0),
