(483641, 44898, 13403, '<td valign="top">ah, fragile.. there is more here than meets the eye.   The definition of irony that I''m using (verbal irony) is: The use of words to express something different from and often opposite to their literal meaning.  or:  An expression or utterance marked by a deliberate contrast between apparent and intended meaning.<br/> <br/>the apparent meaning: (or reason) the manufacturers decided to use the brand-name "Futuro" to peddle their wheelchairs.  It sounds almost something of an optimistic outlook on the future.  But who looks forward to the future when the future seems to mean hinderance.  Frailty, helplessness, and all things inevitable until death..<br/> <br/>also- the irony in using a photograph of a wheelchair for a ''still life'' challenge..    <br/> <br/>thanks for attacking me :)</td>', 'ah, fragile.. there is more here than meets the eye.   The definition of irony that I''m using (verbal irony) is: The use of words to express something different from and often opposite to their literal meaning.  or:  An expression or utterance marked by a deliberate contrast between apparent and intended meaning. the apparent meaning: (or reason) the manufacturers decided to use the brand-name "Futuro" to peddle their wheelchairs.  It sounds almost something of an optimistic outlook on the future.  But who looks forward to the future when the future seems to mean hinderance.  Frailty, helplessness, and all things inevitable until death.. also- the irony in using a photograph of a wheelchair for a ''still life'' challenge..     thanks for attacking me :)', '2003-11-13 03:10:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(483808, 44986, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BobsterLobster:</b></div><hr/><i>A wonderful and beautiful photo, but I don''t see this as a still life. Sorry. 1</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>A 1 is a bit harsh isn''t it? I can understand you maybe thinking this doesn''t meeting the challenge, that is a matter of opinion. But why a 1? You said yourself this is a wonderful and beautiful pic, where are the points for that?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-11-13 07:05:26.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by BobsterLobster:A wonderful and beautiful photo, but I don''t see this as a still life. Sorry. 1  A 1 is a bit harsh isn''t it? I can understand you maybe thinking this doesn''t meeting the challenge, that is a matter of opinion. But why a 1? You said yourself this is a wonderful and beautiful pic, where are the points for that?', '2003-11-13 07:05:05.000000', '2003-11-13 07:05:26.000000', 0),
(483861, 45388, 13827, '<td valign="top">The color is dull because it was such a dreary day that i took the photo.. Too me the flat colors represent a Memory... Hence the darkness of it all... the older memories get the darker they become... yes i could have used something to bring more out in the photo... but i wanted to keep it simple... thanks to everyone for their comments... they are appreciated...</td>', 'The color is dull because it was such a dreary day that i took the photo.. Too me the flat colors represent a Memory... Hence the darkness of it all... the older memories get the darker they become... yes i could have used something to bring more out in the photo... but i wanted to keep it simple... thanks to everyone for their comments... they are appreciated...', '2003-11-13 08:23:12.000000', NULL, 0),
